From 88b6461e73e46ecb94766846868e84d559464e7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CufeHaco <redeagleteam2005@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:38:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Match MRI across library/socket

Outside #9040's scope: everything spec/ruby/library/socket still found
once UNIX sockets were moved, fixed against MRI 4.0.5 (which passes all
of it on the same host). Most of it also fails on stock JRuby.

- send/recv flags (MSG_PEEK, MSG_OOB, ...), recv's outbuf argument,
  sendmsg/recvmsg(_nonblock) with ancillary data, Socket#recvfrom on
  every socket type, Socket#listen/accept/sysaccept on a raw Socket,
  getpeereid and ioctl with a String argument, through FFM on the real
  fd.
- getsockopt/setsockopt go to the kernel when FFM is available, except
  SO_RCVTIMEO/SO_SNDTIMEO, SO_ERROR and IP_ADD_MEMBERSHIP, which stay
  emulated on java.nio. Option takes integer levels and names.
- Blocking FFM calls use MSG_DONTWAIT and wait in waitFd, so Thread#kill,
  Thread#raise and Timeout wake them. Blocking UDP receives wait the same
  way; they could not be interrupted before (stock too).
- Packed sockaddrs use the platform's real struct layout (native-order
  family, sin6_flowinfo), since they now reach the kernel.
- Addresses and names: unbound INET local_address/getsockname, IPv6
  text form, nil host meaning loopback of either family,
  do_not_reverse_lookup per socket, getservbyport, Socket::ResolutionError,
  AI_* / EAI_* / Linux constants, Addrinfo marshal and inspect, shutdown
  argument checks, write_nonblock leaving the socket's mode alone,
  EDESTADDRREQ for send on an unconnected datagram socket.

BasicSocket#sockBits caches per-socket facts (unix, datagram, native fd)
once and reads them without a lock, the same shape as Builtins.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
